---
import './freshness.css';
---
<figure class="fresh-figure">
 <div class="figure-heading"><span class="figure-number">Figure 4</span>Keep the repair work with the source change</div>
 <div class="scene">
  <div class="box changed"><p class="label">One source transaction</p><div class="row"><div><strong>P7 = GBP 22.00</strong><span>revision 2</span></div><div><strong>Change record</strong><span>north / P7 / revision 2</span></div></div><p>Commit both, or neither.</p></div>
  <p class="label">After commit ↓</p>
  <div class="row"><div class="box"><strong>Consumer reads record</strong><span>Delete the product card and affected lists.</span></div><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="box"><strong>Deletion fails</strong><span>Keep the record pending. Retry later.</span></div></div>
  <div class="row"><div class="box"><strong>Deletion succeeds</strong><span>A crash before acknowledgement can cause a repeat.</span></div><span class="arrow" aria-hidden="true">→</span><div class="box"><strong>Mark work complete</strong><span>Continue from the recorded position.</span></div></div>
  <p class="callout">The record survives a stopped application. Until it is processed, readers can still find the old copy.</p>
 </div>
 <figcaption>A transactional outbox used to drive invalidation. The drawing closes the gap between committing a change and recording the work to notify caches. It leaves delivery delay and the late-fill race visible.</figcaption>
</figure>
